warning[temp_storage_escape]: `tprint` holds temporary storage, which is reset, but it is kept in a global
  --> tests/lint/temp_storage_escape/bad.jai:13:21
   |
13 |     current_label = tprint("item %", id);
   |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |                     -------------------- temporary storage allocated here
   |
   = help: copy it first (`copy_string`) so it outlives the reset
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/temp_storage_escape

warning[temp_storage_escape]: `tprint` holds temporary storage, which is reset, but it is kept in a global
  --> tests/lint/temp_storage_escape/bad.jai:22:26
   |
22 |     array_add(*registry, tprint("id %", id));
   |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |                          ------------------ temporary storage allocated here
   |
   = help: copy it first (`copy_string`) so it outlives the reset
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/temp_storage_escape

warning[temp_storage_escape]: `tprint` holds temporary storage, which is reset, but it is returned here
  --> tests/lint/temp_storage_escape/bad.jai:26:12
   |
26 |     return tprint("<%>", id);
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |            ----------------- temporary storage allocated here
   |
   = help: copy it (`copy_string`), or declare this procedure `@TempAllocates` so its callers know
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/temp_storage_escape
